diff --git a/docs/android-stability-phase1.md b/docs/android-stability-phase1.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2a21a4d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/android-stability-phase1.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Android stability: native lifecycle fixes
+
+Base fork commit: 14955e5f2c5f6fe9317314a64845bcc555c808a1.
+
+This Android-only batch is independent of the Linux phase-2 patch. It fixes:
+
+- Recursive acquisition of the non-recursive video codec mutex when a Surface
+  is removed, and the null-Surface path that returned without unlocking.
+- Stop flags, finite output polling and joining output workers before codec
+  stop/delete for both video and audio. No input/EOS availability is required
+  to request cancellation. Driver calls themselves are not hard-time bounded.
+- Native window initialization, release on shutdown and checked surface swaps.
+- Video callbacks falsely returning success for an absent codec or failed
+  queueInputBuffer. Input buffer pointers/capacity and format allocation checked.
+- Audio input error returning without releasing its mutex.
+- Audio format reconfiguration joining while the outer mutex was held.
+- Audio configure/start/thread-creation failure cleanup, output callback guard,
+  PCM offset/range validation and input pointer/capacity checks.
+- Oboe open failure falling through to stream->start().
+- ViewModel cleanup referencing an unused nullable session instead of the real one.
+
+Lifecycle ownership is still serialized by the existing Kotlin/network owners;
+this is not a new general concurrent lifecycle API. Output dequeues are polled
+with a 10 ms timeout. This removes indefinite application-requested waits, but
+cannot promise a misbehaving platform driver will obey the timeout. Removing
+video Surface currently still destroys the codec, and reconstructing it still
+requires configuration/reference recovery work in a later batch.
+
+Validation: bash test/run-android-lifecycle-tests.sh builds the actual video and
+native audio decoder C files with real pthread wrappers and deterministic fake
+NDK objects. It exercises 30 video cycles, 30 audio reconfiguration cycles,
+failed input/queue/surface/configure/start operations, cross-thread lock access,
+and native resource balance. ASan/UBSan enabled; leak detection disabled because
+process inspection is restricted. Resource counts are explicitly asserted.
+
+Not validated: real MediaCodec/vendor behavior, Kotlin or Oboe compilation,
+Oboe stream routing, physical devices, full APK build, startup/playback latency.
+The mocks do not implement actual codecs. Oboe/Kotlin edits are reviewed source
+changes, not covered by the native C harness.
+
+Remaining: valid Opus CSD handling and PLC; compressed access-unit boundaries;
+codec error recovery; asynchronous session disposal; bounded receive/decode
+queues; timestamps and presentation; output-route recovery and audio latency;
+JNI diagnostics and Android settings for congestion/IDR. No claim of completed
+Android stability optimization is made by this batch.
